b  parts of it are very disappointingly  greedy or underwhelming  but i feel like at some point down the  line this game was made with a lot of  love and passion these linear levels  where you get to explore a character's  individual talents and see them  interacting with their super pals in a  creative and fun set piece  these are the real standouts like  captain america and iron man escaping an  exploding satellite  miss marvel running from the hulk after  he thinks she stole cap's shield  iron man exploring around his decaying  family home to build a makeshift suit  and gear up for action or the beginning  and end of the game where you play as  every avenger as they take on a unique  obstacle suited to their skills  parts like these are where i see this  game's untapped potential  this could have been a really amazing  single player experience if the game was  more of that stuff  but as it is it's unfortunately bogged  down by things i want to believe the  game wasn't originally intended to have  the live service elements and  multiplayer elements feel so  underdeveloped and tacked on i started  wondering if they were added later in  development and this game was probably  meant to be something more linear and  toned down  i feel like somewhere down the line  something changed and it lost its  identity but i wasn't part of  development so i can't say for sure  that's just speculation on my part  buried under all this unnecessary fluff  there was the makings of something  special with the end result being a  mixed bag that i think  had more potential and i hope that one  day we do  get the game that this one tried to be  because i have a feeling it came very  close to being something great  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you

